  "preamble": "Loss of the laminal palatal stop *c (often written tj or j) at the start of a word is part of initial dropping in Australian Pama-Nyungan languages. Proto-Pama-Nyungan had no voicing contrast in stops, so *c also covers the sound that other sources write as *ɟ. The stop disappears in Arandic (Arrernte aleñe 'tongue' < *calañ). Proto-Dravidian initial *c, reconstructed as a palatal stop, was lost in many words in Tamil, Malayalam, Kannada, Tulu and Telugu (*cāṯu 'six' > Tamil āṟu, *cup 'salt' > Kannada and Telugu uppu), while Gondi and Kui have s- in the same words.",
  "phoneticEffects": "Elision, Initial Dropping",
